1
00:00:00,720 --> 00:00:22,910
Full of Surprises

2
00:00:22,910 --> 00:00:24,480
Hello. What can I do for you?

3
00:00:24,480 --> 00:00:26,400
Hi. Fill 'er up.

4
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:27,750
I need a full tank.

5
00:00:27,750 --> 00:00:28,870
Check the hood?

6
00:00:28,870 --> 00:00:38,610
No, thanks.

7
00:00:38,610 --> 00:00:40,270
Whereabouts are you headed?

8
00:00:40,270 --> 00:00:43,530
Pete Waters's farm, near Chesterton.

9
00:00:43,530 --> 00:00:45,340
I know it well.

10
00:00:45,340 --> 00:00:49,220
Pete Waters's lived around here almost as long as I have.

11
00:00:49,220 --> 00:00:51,890
How long is it going to take for me to get there?

12
00:00:51,890 --> 00:00:53,700
About fifteen minutes.

13
00:00:53,700 --> 00:00:56,000
There's a shortcut--if you know it.

14
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:57,850
No, I don't.

15
00:00:57,850 --> 00:01:00,290
Could you tell me how to use the shortcut?

16
00:01:00,290 --> 00:01:02,590
Sure. You take the next left turn.

17
00:01:02,590 --> 00:01:04,840
You'll see a stop sign.

18
00:01:04,840 --> 00:01:07,080
Make a right at the stop sign.

19
00:01:07,080 --> 00:01:10,540
Stay on that road, and you'll cross a blue bridge.

20
00:01:10,540 --> 00:01:13,190
Then you'll see a big old red barn.

21
00:01:13,190 --> 00:01:17,050
That's the back of Pete Waters's place.

22
00:01:17,050 --> 00:01:22,760
That's quite a difference from the directions that Pete sent me.

23
00:01:22,760 --> 00:01:26,090
Now, if you take that route, it's probably a lot simpler,

24
00:01:26,090 --> 00:01:30,520
but it'll take you ten minutes longer.

25
00:01:30,520 --> 00:01:34,280
OK. Let me repeat it.

26
00:01:34,280 --> 00:01:38,300
I take the next left turn to the stop sign.

27
00:01:38,300 --> 00:01:42,840
Then a right across a blue bridge,

28
00:01:42,840 --> 00:01:45,360
and then a big red barn.

29
00:01:45,360 --> 00:01:49,960
Can't miss it.

30
00:01:49,960 --> 00:01:51,320
How much do I owe you?

31
00:01:51,320 --> 00:01:56,070
Well, that'll be eighteen dollars and seventy cents.

32
00:01:56,070 --> 00:01:58,280
No charge for the cleanup.

33
00:01:58,280 --> 00:02:01,260
It's on the house.

34
00:02:01,260 --> 00:02:02,780
Well, here's a twenty.

35
00:02:02,780 --> 00:02:11,950
Ah. OK. That's a dollar and thirty cents change.

36
00:02:11,950 --> 00:02:16,380
There we go ... will make twenty. Thanks.

37
00:02:16,380 --> 00:02:17,940
Thank you.

38
00:02:17,940 --> 00:02:57,880
And thanks for the directions.

39
00:02:57,880 --> 00:03:01,020
This must be Pete's barn.

40
00:03:01,020 --> 00:03:13,240
Turn right to the house.

41
00:03:13,240 --> 00:03:13,960
Hi.

42
00:03:13,960 --> 00:03:15,640
Hi. What can I do for you?

43
00:03:15,640 --> 00:03:17,050
Is this the Pete Waters farm?

44
00:03:17,050 --> 00:03:18,520
It is.

45
00:03:18,520 --> 00:03:19,570
I'm a friend of Pete's.

46
00:03:19,570 --> 00:03:20,640
I'm looking for the house.

47
00:03:20,640 --> 00:03:21,820
It's just over yonder.

48
00:03:21,820 --> 00:03:22,770
Keep along this road

49
00:03:22,770 --> 00:03:23,970
till you get to the end of the fence.

50
00:03:23,970 --> 00:03:25,050
You'll see the chicken house.

51
00:03:25,050 --> 00:03:26,570
His house is on the left.

52
00:03:26,570 --> 00:03:58,840
Well, thanks.

53
00:03:58,840 --> 00:04:01,030
"Have gone to the railroad station.

54
00:04:01,030 --> 00:04:03,780
Back soon with a surprise.

55
00:04:03,780 --> 00:04:05,580
Make yourself at home.

56
00:04:05,580 --> 00:04:10,030
Have a look around. Pete.

57
00:04:10,030 --> 00:04:12,260
Same old Pete Waters.

58
00:04:12,260 --> 00:04:15,260
Always full of surprises.
